# An agent profile: Pi on models served by your own machine. Rename to pi.env
# to use it (make init copies this folder to user-config/ for you), then:
#
#   make new WITH="<repo>" AGENT=pi     a sandbox whose own agent is this one
#   make run N=<n>                      creates its VM from this profile
#
# Plain bash, like .env, but only these four settings are allowed; anything
# else is refused. See README.md, "Kit-based agents and profiles".

# What sbx runs: a built-in agent (claude, codex, ...) or a kit reference.
AGENT="dhi.io/pi:latest"

# The agent's arguments, on every make run (before any ARGS="..." given
# then). Empty: the agent's own defaults.
ARGS=""

# sbx run flags for creating the VM, after SBX_CREATE_FLAGS from .env.
# Relative paths are taken from the tool's folder. Never -e, --env or
# --env-file: the agent can read those (they're refused).
CREATE_FLAGS="--kit user-config/kits/pi-local-models --kit-args-file user-config/pi-local-models.args"

# Names of the sbx secrets this agent uses for cloud models, never their
# values: set each on the host with `sbx secret set <name>`, and the VM only
# sees a placeholder. Empty for local models only.
CREDENTIALS=""
